So, what's wrong? The Pex assert failed message doesn't provide any clues about what's actually wrong.

A: Assertion's parameters are not initialized in your test scenario.
From debug message: PexGeneratedException: An assertion failed at line 45, in body of ArrayList.Test.ArrayListContractTest.PUT_AddContract., we can see that the error is thrown on the line 45 of PUT_AddContract method. 

But the problem is that the parameters Old_arrListIndexOfX, Old_arrListLastIndexOfX, minIndexInArrayList and maxIndexInArrayList are not initialized in your code.

You probably forget to add some code in your test to fill these parameters.

Ensure to call Add() method first before the assert. Then these parameters would be initialized.

Additionally to your assertions the conditions are not expressed correctly. If your assertions are like "index_of_x__ge__min_index_in_array_list && index_of_x__le__max_index_in_array_list" and "last_index_of_x__ge__min_index_in_array_list && last_index_of_--------------------	    // which also means that x is added to list at end 
            AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(New_arrListLastIndexOfX>= Old_arrListIndexOfX);

	    // and also x is in the list now.
            AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(New_arrListContainsX == true);

	    // and the count of the list should increased by one
            AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount + 1);

        } 
    }
}

